+## Dormant host integration
+
+A dormant native command boundary can be attached through `NativeCommandBridge`. The UI pre-gate runs before keyboard/IME dispatch, and `Session` checks the complete native document after qualified text/inline commands, restoring all native session bookkeeping on a rejected local command. The exact read/navigation allowlist excludes external window/file actions. Attachment refuses existing native recovery without consuming pending copies; attached recovery ticks cannot adopt or persist an asynchronous document. Proposal capture follows validation; failed capture retains a visible unsaved draft and blocks further editing. The seam supplies no SDK implementation, transport, authority, receipt or collaborative undo policy.
+
+The explicit `?mooring=1` web entry waits for one local SDK bootstrap instead of opening a blank/sample document. Its caller supplies untouched native JSON and stable paragraph IDs; browser credentials, WebSockets and receipt authority remain outside WordApp. The local bridge can project only existing paragraph text/runs after a complete native equality check, retaining session/document identity, and can delegate outer undo/redo to the original SDK controller. It never runs native file-history undo in this mode. Unsupported structural changes, file replacement, drop/picture paste and native recovery remain excluded; failed capture preserves an unsaved Draft. Actual browser transport, authenticated multiplayer, host Saved and overlapping-delete undo are still unqualified.
